├── Project.toml

├── src/

│   └── ThermodynamicModel.jl  (The main entry point)

├── sub_modules/

│   └── FugacityCo/

│       ├── Project.toml

│       └── src/

│           └── FugacityCo.jl


Okay I actually have it structured like this


now I need to reconcile the include and using statements

To reconcile your statements in this nested structure, you need to transition from "File Loading" (using include) to "Package Loading" (using using).

In a nested structure, Julia doesn't automatically "see" the sub_modules just because they are in the folder. You have to tell the main project that FugacityCo is a dependency it should track.
Step 1: "Develop" the Sub-Module

You must link the sub-module to your main project so Julia knows where to find it. Open your Julia REPL in the Thermodynamic Model folder and run these commands:
Julia

# 1. Activate the main project
import Pkg; Pkg.activate(".")

# 2. Tell the main project to "track" the sub-module folder
Pkg.develop(path="sub_modules/FugacityCo")

Note: This adds a [deps] entry to your main Project.toml. You only need to do this once.
