Summary of the "Rules"

    The src Folder: Any file inside the same src folder as the module file should be loaded with include("file.jl").

    The Sub-Modules: Any folder that has its own Project.toml and src folder is treated as a separate Package. You load these with using after "developing" the path.

Why this satisfies the "Folder Shifter"

By using Pkg.develop(path="..."), Julia records a relative path in your Manifest.toml. As long as the user keeps the sub_modules folder inside the Thermodynamic Model folder, they can move the entire project to a different drive or computer, and it will still work perfectly.

