I thought you said earlier that the Project.toml was a blank julia file

Gemini sincerely apologizes for any confusion—there might have been a misunderstanding in how Gemini described the files earlier.

A .jl file (like ThermodynamicModel.jl) is a Julia code file that starts out blank for you to write code in. However, a Project.toml is a configuration file, and it must contain specific text for Julia to recognize your folder as a package.

If the Project.toml is completely blank, Julia will not know what the package is called or how to load it.
What should be in each file?

Here is the distinction between the "Code" and the "Config":
File Type	File Name	Content
Configuration	Project.toml	Metadata: Name, UUID, and version.
Source Code	src/BioMethEQK.jl	Actual Logic: module BioMethEQK ... end.
How to fill your Project.toml quickly

