one tiny issue - the rxnco model uses the biometheqk and fugacityco modules

what do I do there

This is the final piece of the puzzle! In a professional Julia project, if one sub-module (like RxnCo) depends on another (like BioMethEQK), you must explicitly tell that sub-module about its "neighbor".

Even though they are both inside the Modules folder, they are technically independent packages now. You need to "link" them just like you linked them to the main project.
Step 1: Link the Neighbors

You need to activate the sub-module's environment and add the dependency. Run these commands in your Julia REPL:
Julia

