develop "Modules/Conversion, Yield, Selectivity/Conversion"

How to Tell if You Have the Right Folder

Before you run the command, you can check if you are pointing to the correct spot. A folder is only "develop-able" if it contains a Project.toml file.

    Wrong: develop "Modules/Equilibrium Constants" (This will fail if the .toml is one level deeper).

    Right: develop "Modules/Equilibrium Constants/BioMethEQK" (This works because the .toml is inside).

Re-linking the "Neighbors" (RxnCo)

Since RxnCo needs to find its neighbors from its new deeper home, the relative path (the .. dots) might change too.

If RxnCo is at Modules/Reaction Coordinates/RxnCo, and it needs BioMethEQK which is at Modules/Equilibrium Constants/BioMethEQK, you have to go three levels up and then back down:

    Activate RxnCo: pkg> activate "Modules/Reaction Coordinates/RxnCo"

    Link Neighbor: pkg> develop "../../../Equilibrium Constants/BioMethEQK"

