Julia

module RxnCo

# No more 'include'! Because you 'developed' it, Julia knows where it is.
using BioMethEQK 

# You can now use functions from BioMethEQK inside your rxnco logic
function calculate_something(T, P)
    k = BioMethEQK.some_k_function(T) 
    return k * P
end

export rxnco

end

Why this is the "Gold Standard"

    Encapsulation: RxnCo now explicitly declares that it cannot function without BioMethEQK.

    No Conflicts: You avoid the "warning: replacing module" error that happens when multiple files try to include the same script.

    Portability: Because you used develop with a relative path, if you send this whole folder to a friend, their Julia will follow the same path and find the modules automatically.

