Let’s stop messing around with the command line and ../../ paths. We are going to force-fix this using a single "Repair Script" that calculates the paths for you.
The "Nuclear Option" Repair Script

Please create a new file named fix_project.jl in your main Thermodynamic Model folder (right next to your main Project.toml). Paste this exact code into it:
Julia

import Pkg

# 1. Get the absolute path of your current folder to avoid any ".." confusion
ROOT_PATH = pwd() 

println("🔧 Starting Repair Process...")
println("Root detected at: $ROOT_PATH")

# ===================================================
# FIXING RXNCO DEPENDENCIES
# ===================================================
println("\n1️⃣  Fixing RxnCo dependencies...")

# Path to the RxnCo environment
rxnco_env = joinpath(ROOT_PATH, "Modules", "Reaction Coordinates", "RxnCo")
Pkg.activate(rxnco_env)

# Define exact paths to the neighbors
biometh_path = joinpath(ROOT_PATH, "Modules", "Equilibrium Constants", "BioMethEQK")
fugacity_path = joinpath(ROOT_PATH, "Modules", "Fugacity Coefficients", "FugacityCo")

# Force-develop them
println("   Linking BioMethEQK...")
Pkg.develop(path=biometh_path)

println("   Linking FugacityCo...")
Pkg.develop(path=fugacity_path)

# Ensure standard packages are present
println("   Adding NLsolve and Reexport...")
Pkg.add(["NLsolve", "Reexport", "Printf"])

Pkg.resolve()
Pkg.instantiate()

# ===================================================
# RETURN TO MAIN PROJECT
# ===================================================
println("\n2️⃣  Returning to Main Project...")
Pkg.activate(ROOT_PATH)
Pkg.resolve()
Pkg.instantiate()

println("\n✅ REPAIR COMPLETE. Try running your Test Case now.")

How to Run It

    Open your terminal/REPL in the Thermodynamic Model folder.

    Run: include("fix_project.jl")

Why this will work

This script bypasses the manual pkg> mode. It uses absolute paths generated by Julia itself (joinpath) to find the folders. It doesn't matter if there are spaces, or if you are one level up or down. It forces RxnCo to recognize its neighbors.

After you run this, open that RxnCo/Project.toml file again. You will see BioMethEQK and FugacityCo appear in the [deps] list automatically.

